Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.40,0:00:05.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandmother said an emperor\Ncamped under Mount Tossa saw a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.69,0:00:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,comet, and named the\Nplace Dessie: my joy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.40,0:00:17.15,Default,,0,0,0,,At seven, I made a comet of my\Nown: old socks, plastic bags
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.15,0:00:18.43,Default,,0,0,0,,and string.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.40,0:00:24.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing in Dessie is flat.\NEven our football pitch
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.10,0:00:26.12,Default,,0,0,0,,climbed the mountain.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.40,0:00:32.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Our rule: kick it in the\Nditch, you climb in after it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.66,0:00:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Hayat's left foot is the\Nreason that rule exists.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.19,0:00:45.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Four–four. Next goal wins.\NThen the fog came down from
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.22,0:00:48.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Tossa like a white gabi.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.19,0:00:54.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I couldn't see anything but my\Ncomet. I kicked it with all I
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.48,0:00:59.13,Default,,0,0,0,,had. It vanished into the\Nfog. “GOAL!” shouted Dawit.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.90,0:01:05.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandmother laughed and pulled\Nme under her gabi: “A comet
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.68,0:01:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,doesn't stay. It only shows\Nyou where your joy is.”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.53,0:01:15.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, when people ask where\NI'm from, I say Dessie. And
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.87,0:01:18.24,Default,,0,0,0,,then I tell them\Nwhat it means.
